{"seq":1,"mint":"C14","verb":"claim","status":"ok","model":"openai/gpt-5.6-luna","approach":"split","literals":true,"findings":[{"kind":"contradicts","clause":"An absolute label is structural","clause_quoted":true,"facts":[],"why":"The look label is built from the caller-provided path string, while relative paths are accepted and resolved; absolute-ness is therefore determined by the caller's spelling, not structurally enforced.","quoted":false,"rejected_span":"        let (shown, label) = match lines {\n        None => (contents.clone(), path.to_string()),\n\n//! Every path a tool takes (`look`'s `path`, `render`'s `out`,\n//! `check`/`brief`/`record`'s memo) is resolved against **this server's**\n//! working directory, which is wherever the client happened to start it —\n//! not the caller's, and not anything the caller can see or set. A\n//! relative path therefore resolves somewhere the caller cannot predict."},{"kind":"contradicts","clause":"not an authoring mistake.","clause_quoted":true,"facts":[],"why":"Because the label preserves the caller's path spelling and the server handles relative paths rather than rejecting them, a relative label can result from the author's supplied path.","quoted":false,"rejected_span":"        let (shown, label) = match lines {\n        None => (contents.clone(), path.to_string()),\n\n//! Every path a tool takes (`look`'s `path`, `render`'s `out`,\n//! `check`/`brief`/`record`'s memo) is resolved against **this server's**\n//! working directory, which is wherever the client happened to start it —\n//! not the caller's, and not anything the caller can see or set. A\n//! relative path therefore resolves somewhere the caller cannot predict."},{"kind":"contradicts","clause":"No amount of author care can produce a relative label over MCP.","clause_quoted":true,"facts":[],"why":"MCP does not enforce absolute input: it resolves relative paths, and look labels use the supplied path string unchanged. A caller supplying a relative path can